    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSTUNNING SEASIDE ESTATE WITH HUGE REDEVELOPMENT POTENTIAL on c. 8.85 ACRES AT FURBO, CO GALWAY. \n\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are honoured to present for sale by Private Treaty, an exceptional detached coastal residence enjoying one of the most spectacular waterfront positions on Galway Bay at Aillepreachain, Furbo.\n\nExtending to approximately 357.9 sq.m. (3,852 sq.ft.) and standing on approximately 3.58 hectares (8.85 acres) of mature private grounds, this unique property commands breathtaking panoramic sea views, benefits from direct private access to Furbo Beach, and offers an increasingly rare opportunity to acquire a substantial coastal holding in one of Galway's most sought-after seaside locations, just a short stroll from the village.\n\nApproached by a sweeping driveway and surrounded by mature trees and beautifully established gardens, Aillepreachain offers an exceptional sense of peace and privacy. The grounds gently extend towards the shoreline where a private gate opens directly onto Furbo Beach, allowing the beach to become part of everyday life. Morning walks along the shore, a refreshing swim in Galway Bay or simply sitting by the water's edge become effortless, creating a lifestyle that few properties can offer.\n\nThe residence has been carefully positioned to embrace its spectacular surroundings. Large picture windows frame breathtaking views across Galway Bay, while the expansive first-floor balcony provides an ever-changing outlook over the water, from tranquil summer mornings to dramatic Atlantic sunsets. Whether relaxing indoors or outside, the sea is a constant presence, creating a home that is deeply connected to its surroundings.\n\nExtending over two floors, the residence offers generous family accommodation comprising seven bedrooms and a number of spacious reception rooms. While the property would benefit from refurbishment and modernisation, it presents an exceptional opportunity to restore and enhance a substantial home in a setting that is truly irreplaceable. Properties can be renovated and reimagined, but opportunities to acquire an extensive beachfront holding of this nature are exceptionally rare.\n\nAillepreachain is just a short stroll from the renowned Pádraicíns Gastropub, while a footpath leads to the centre of Furbo village, approximately 1 km away, where a range of local amenities, schools and services are available. Galway City is also within easy reach, offering the perfect balance between peaceful coastal living and everyday convenience.\n\nCombining approximately 3.58 hectares (8.85 acres) of private coastal grounds, direct access onto Furbo Beach, panoramic views across Galway Bay and a substantial detached residence with outstanding potential, Aillepreachain represents one of the most unique waterfront opportunities to come to the Galway market in recent years."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nA welcoming entrance hall provides access to the principal reception rooms and ground floor accommodation.\n\nKitchen / Dining Area - \nPositioned to the front of the property, the kitchen is fitted with a selection of fitted units offering ample storage and workspace. The dining area is set on an elevated level, creating a wonderful space to dine while enjoying beautiful views across Galway Bay.\n\nGuest Shower Room - \nConveniently located off the entrance hall, this fully tiled shower room comprises a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nDining Room - \nA well-proportioned formal dining room, ideal for entertaining family and friends or special occasions.\n\nLiving Room - \nA spacious reception room enjoying exceptional views across Galway Bay, with double doors opening onto the front terrace and gardens. The room features two fireplaces and offers excellent proportions, presenting wonderful potential for modernisation while making the most of its remarkable coastal setting.\n\nRear Hall - \nA spacious rear hallway providing access to all four ground floor bedrooms, the family bathroom, separate WC and the staircase to the first floor. The hall also benefits from useful understairs storage together with an external door leading to the side of the property.\n\nBathroom - \nFully tiled with a bath and wash hand basin\n\nSeparate WC - \nFully tiled with a WC and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nA comfortable double bedroom overlooking the front terrace.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nA comfortable double bedroom overlooking the mature side gardens.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nA generously proportioned double bedroom enjoying beautiful views across Galway Bay.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nAnother spacious double bedroom with wonderful sea views overlooking the gardens and coastline.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - \nProviding access to the first-floor accommodation.\n\nBedroom 5 - \nA generously proportioned double bedroom with views over the surrounding grounds and the benefit of an en-suite shower room.\n\nEn-Suite - \nFully tiled with a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 6 - \nA spacious double bedroom overlooking the side of the property, complete with an en-suite shower room.\n\nEn-Suite - \nFully tiled with a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nPrincipal Bedroom - \nAn exceptionally spacious double bedroom enjoying spectacular panoramic views across Galway Bay. This impressive room benefits from a private balcony, creating the perfect space to take in the breathtaking coastal setting, together with an en-suite shower room.\n\nEn-Suite - \nFully tiled with a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nA spacious, fully tiled bathroom complete with a Jacuzzi bath, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nFirst Floor Living Room - \nThe standout room of the property, this spacious first-floor living room enjoys panoramic views across Galway Bay through large picture windows and double doors opening onto the expansive balcony. A feature fireplace creates a central focal point, while the elevated position makes this an exceptional space to relax and enjoy the ever-changing coastal scenery.\n\nGarage - \nAccessed externally beneath the kitchen, the garage provides excellent storage and houses the oil-fired central heating boiler.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> c. 3.58 hectares (8.85 acres) of exceptional coastal grounds.</li><li> Private gate opening directly onto Furbo Beach.</li><li> Spectacular panoramic views across Galway Bay.</li><li> Detached residence extending to c. 357.9 sq.m. (3,852 sq.ft.)</li><li> Seven-bedroom family home with outstanding potential.</li><li> Expansive first-floor balcony overlooking the bay.</li><li> Mature gardens and grounds stretching to the shoreline.</li><li> A short stroll to Pádraicíns Gastropub.</li><li> Footpath to Furbo Village and local amenities.</li><li> A truly unique waterfront property in a highly sought-after coastal location.</ul>"
